cts, explain implication.\n\nWe should consider all candidates now. Let's evaluate:\n\nCandidate A: strengths: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. No explicit reliability, stress resilience, attention, communication. Leadership good but show-off? Not in notes. Might be less reliable.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), weak memory for numbers (attention), communication issues (nasty remarks, pretentious). Adaptability unknown.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), difficulty communicating ideas (communication), egocentric (crew), not willing to further education (adaptability), known 100% reliable (reliability), creates positive atmosphere (crew cooperation), excellent attention skills (attention). Stress resilience? Not explicit but \"calm in crisis\"? Not in notes. But we have \"makes correct decisions quickly\" maybe implies calm.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical/decision), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), hot temper, arrogant (crew cooperation, communication), weak leadership.\n\nNow we have more info: B's attention mixed, C's attention excellent, D's attention good, A unknown.\n\nWe need to decide recommendation. Which candidate best fits overall? Let's weigh:\n\nReliability: B (very conscientious), C (100% reliable), D (responsibility serious), A unknown.\n\nStress resilience: B (handles stress well), D (responds adequately), C unknown, A unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: D (solves problems extremely well), B (good at weather, computer), C (makes correct decisions quickly), A (sees complex connections, spatial vision).\n\nDecision quality: C (quick correct decisions), D (problem solving), B unknown, A unknown.\n\nAttention: C excellent, D very good, B weak memory for numbers, A unknown.\n\nCrew cooperation: C creates positive atmosphere, B uncooperative/nasty remarks, D arrogant, A unknown.\n\nCommunication: C difficulty communicating, B nasty remarks, D arrogant, A unknown.\n\nResponsibility: D serious, B conscientious, C reliable, A leadership.\n\nAdaptability: B unknown, C not willing to further education (low), D unknown, A not open to new ideas (low), B unknown.\n\nOverall, C has strong reliability, attention, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric, plus low adaptability. D has strong technical, responsibility, attention, but hot temper and arrogance. B has reliability, stress, but attention weakness and communication issues. A has leadership but many unknowns.\n\nWhich candidate best overall? Might be C because reliability, attention, crew atmosphere, decision quality, but communication difficulty is serious. However, his egocentric and not willing to further education may be problematic. D's hot temper could be dangerous under stress. B's attention weakness could affect safety.\n\nGiven the safety-critical nature, crew cooperation and communication are vital. C creates positive atmosphere but difficulty communicating ideas may hinder. However, positive atmosphere suggests good crew cooperation despite communication difficulty. B's uncooperative and nasty remarks are more severe. D's arrogance and hot temper also severe.\n\nThus C might be the best despite adaptability concerns. But we have no explicit stress resilience for C. However, quick correct decisions may imply calmness.\n\nWe need to make a contribution: perhaps propose Candidate C as the leading candidate, citing reliability, attention, positive crew atmosphere, decision quality, and note concerns about communication and adaptability but argue they are manageable.\n\nWe should reference previous discussion: Agent 2 recommended D, Agent 3 recommended B. We'll argue that C's strengths outweigh D and B's concerns.\n\nProvide explicit facts: known 100% reliable, excellent attention skills, creates positive atmosphere, can make correct decisions quickly. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nExplain why still best: reliability, attention, decision quality are core, crew atmosphere positive, and communication can be trained.\n\nThus vote for Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
